<title>ISRAEL: Teva gets approval for Trazodone.</title>
<headline>Teva gets approval for Trazodone.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-05-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Teva Pharmaceutical Industries received approval from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration to manufacture and market Trazodone 150 mg tablets, the Israeli company said in a statement on Sunday.</p>
<p>Teva previously received FDA approval for 50 mg and 100 mg dosage strength.</p>
<p>Trazodone is the generic equivalent of Bristol Myers Squibb Co's Desyrel, an antidepressant with U.S. sales of about $33 million a year.</p>
<p>-Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211</p>
